  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A sample of an ideal gas is taken through the cyclic process <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>A</mi></math> as shown in figure. It absorbs, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math> of heat during the part <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math>, no heat during <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> and rejects <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math> of heat during <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mi>A</mi></math>. A work of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math> is done on the gas during the part <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>. The internal energy of the gas at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1560</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>. The work done by the gas during the part <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mi>A</mi></math> is</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/a34d352d-82ef-450a-a47a-09a0cf5845cc-image.png\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 150px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "9Co2B",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "enknQ",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
